# Paths that can hold state that matters: accounts, credentials, keys and
# database content. bt-layer-measure never subtracts a difference at one of
# these because it fell inside the noise floor. It keeps their bytes at
# capture time and compares them in both pairs, so a clock that moves in
# every build is reported as noise while an account that is gone in one
# build is reported as real.
#
# The rule this list exists for: for the mariadb component the noise floor
# was 179 files of which 173 were ./var/lib/mysql/**, and that directory
# holds mysql/global_priv and mysql/user.*, so the measurement of a
# component whose build-time job includes deleting accounts was blind
# exactly where the accounts live.
#
# One bash glob per line; * crosses a slash, so ** and * are the same thing
# here and ** is written where a whole subtree is meant. Adding a path is
# cheap: it costs a copy of the file in each capture and a byte comparison.

# accounts and credentials
./etc/shadow
./etc/gshadow
./etc/passwd
./etc/group
./etc/subuid
./etc/subgid
./etc/sudoers
./etc/sudoers.d/**
./etc/security/opasswd

# host and user keys
./etc/ssh/ssh_host_*
./root/.ssh/**
./home/**/.ssh/**
./etc/ssl/private/**

# database state
./var/lib/mysql/**
./var/lib/postgresql/**
./var/lib/redis/**
./var/lib/couchdb/**
./var/lib/mongodb/**

# application and console accounts
./etc/webmin/miniserv.users
./etc/webmin/miniserv.conf
./var/lib/nodebb/**
./etc/keel/instance.d/**
